  "content": {
    "id": "p61-q30-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "30",
    "prompt": "Given $f(x)=\\dfrac{2x}{x+3}$, find $x$ if $f'(x)=\\dfrac{1}{6}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=-9$ or $x=3$.",
      "worked": "Using the quotient rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}\nf'(x)&=\\frac{2(x+3)-2x}{(x+3)^2}\\\\\nf'(x)&=\\frac{6}{(x+3)^2}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nSet the derivative equal to $\\dfrac{1}{6}$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{6}{(x+3)^2}&=\\frac{1}{6}\\\\\n(x+3)^2&=36\\\\\nx+3&=\\pm6\\\\\nx&=-9\\text{ or }3.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
